/*
# ProgressBar

Display-only bounded number — the read-only sibling of Slider (same `value`/
`min`/`max` vocabulary, no interaction, no `input`). Restyle by theme; set
`width` at the use site (220 by default).

## value
Where the bar sits, in the units you choose. Clamped into `min`…`max` for display,
so a value outside the range renders full or empty rather than overflowing.

## min
The value that reads as empty. Defaults to 0.

## max
The value that reads as full. Defaults to 100 — set it to your own total and pass
raw counts as `value` rather than converting to a percentage yourself.

## fill
The track wears the quiet control tint; the filled part is the bar's own child in the accent, so a theme restyles both at once.

## theme
The provided design-token record this widget styles off — a **provided value**
(the app provides it once with `App [ theme = { … } ]`; `Control` and the library
widgets read it). Reads `theme.accent` and its kin as typed members; defaults to the
house look. See `Control.theme`.
*/

class ProgressBar extends View [
    // The design-token record, a provided value: the app provides it once and
    // this widget reads it, so `theme.x` reads below are plain typed members.
    // Default = the house look.

    theme: Theme = { provided("theme", SanFrancisco) },
    width = 220, height = 8, cornerRadius = 4,
    value: number = 0,
    min:   number = 0,
    max:   number = 100,

    fill = { theme.control },

    bar: View [ height = 100%, cornerRadius = 4, fill = { theme.accent },
        width = { parent.width * Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (value - min) / ((max - min) || 1))) } ]
    ]
